# prologue.vn — CUDA HEARTS opening scene
#
# Format reference (see README):
#   ~ scene <id>            background switch
#   ~ show <cast> [mood]    put a character on stage
#   ~ hide <cast>           remove from stage
#   ~ label <name>          branch target
#   ~ jump <name>           go to label
#   ~ affinity <+n|-n>      relationship score
#   ~ flag <name>           story flag
#   ~ ending <name>         reach an ending
#   <speaker>: text         dialogue (speaker must be in vn::cast)
#   * text -> label         choice option (consecutive * lines = one block)

~ scene gtc_backstage
narrator: GTC. Nine thousand developers, one leather jacket, and you — holding two backstage passes you definitely did not win legally.

~ show jensen neutral
jensen: The more you buy, the more you save.

narrator: He says it to the espresso machine. It still works on you.

you: That's... not how discounts work.

~ show jensen happy
jensen: That's not how GPU physics works either, and yet here we are.

narrator: Somewhere behind him, a demo rack spins up on its own, like a jukebox that knows.

* Flirt with silicon metaphors -> flirt
* Ask about the jacket -> jacket
* Play it safe -> safe

~ label flirt
~ affinity +2
~ flag cuda_rizz
you: Are you a data center? Because my heart just doubled its throughput.
~ show jensen happy
jensen: Careful. The more you love, the more you save.
~ jump encore

~ label jacket
~ affinity +1
~ flag jacket_lore
you: Is the jacket load-bearing at this point?
jensen: It has outlasted four CEOs and one cryptocurrency winter.
narrator: He says this with the gravity of a man reading his own keynote.
~ jump encore

~ label safe
you: Mr. Huang, I'm actually here about the conference badge mix-up.
~ show jensen neutral
jensen: A shame. The espresso machine was starting to open up.
~ jump encore

~ label encore
~ scene rooftop
~ show jensen neutral
~ hide crowd
narrator: He hands you half of a warm taiyaki. The city glows green below, like a very serious RGB build.
jensen: Same time next keynote?

~ ending first_keynote
